      <p>I'm a wedding and quinceañera photographer. I built MomentCast to stream my own clients' events, then opened it up to other photographers and videographers. This guide is what I'd tell a second shooter before their first stream.</p>

      <p>My rig is modest. Two Sony cameras, Hollyland wireless video transmitters, an ATEM Mini switcher, a Zoom H4 for audio, and OBS Studio on a Windows laptop. I use OBS for the examples here, but nothing in MomentCast is OBS-only. If you run vMix, Wirecast, Streamlabs, or a hardware encoder, the settings are the same and only the menu names change. Throughout this guide, "encoder" means whatever software or box sends your video out.</p>

